  WHAT THE MEASUREMENT CHANGES ABOUT THE PLAN'S PROJECTION
  -------------------------------------------------------
  The plan carried V = 474 395, G = 411 330, L ~ 31 000 and expected the
  kMaxVoices choice to be decisive on a 645 ns/spare-slot margin. MEASURED
  L = 12 692.4 - LESS THAN HALF the projected spare-slot cost. Therefore:

    * at polyphony 4, lowering kMaxVoices 8 -> 6 saves     25 385 ns = 0.79 % of ref
    * at polyphony 4, lowering kMaxVoices 8 -> 4 saves     50 770 ns = 1.59 % of ref

  L-7 does not change a single verdict in the tables above: N_ref and N_gate are
  identical at kMaxVoices 4, 6 and 8. The lever is nearly free to apply and
  nearly worthless as a budget instrument. The plan's expectation that
  "polyphony 4 clears the gated line only with L-4 applied and kMaxVoices at 6"
  is FALSIFIED by the measurement in both directions: kMaxVoices is not the
  lever, and L-4 alone is not enough either (SECTION 3).

================================================================================
SECTION 3 - what SC-001b would actually require at each candidate polyphony
================================================================================

  SC-001b (spec.md:1375-1383) has TWO clauses:
    (i)  measured <= kReferenceNs      = 3 200 000
    (ii) checked-in baseline, = ceil(measured x 1.05) (FR-083, spec.md:1244),
         <= kMaxAdmissibleNs           = 2 133 333
  Clause (ii) binds first: it caps the MEASURED figure at 2 133 333 / 1.05 =
  2 031 746 ns/block.

    poly | measured + Cavern | clause (i)  | baseline ceil(x1.05) | clause (ii)
    -----+-------------------+-------------+----------------------+-------------
      1  |   991 908         | PASS  31.0 %|   1 041 504          | PASS  48.8 %
      2  | 1 521 090         | PASS  47.5 %|   1 597 145          | PASS  74.9 %
      4  | 2 704 220         | PASS  84.5 %|   2 839 431          | FAIL 133.1 %
      6  | 3 596 160         | FAIL 112.4 %|  3 775 968           | FAIL 177.0 %
      8  | 4 585 300         | FAIL 143.3 %|  4 814 565           | FAIL 225.7 %

  READ ROW 4 TWICE. At the roadmap's own floor of 4 voices the instrument
  ALREADY MEETS roadmap line 470's 30 %-of-a-core ceiling (84.5 % of it, i.e.
  25.4 % of one core, everything on, cavern included). What it does not meet is
  the repo's internal regression-headroom convention, kMaxAdmissibleNs =
  kReferenceNs / 1.5, which FR-083 applies to the CHECKED-IN BASELINE.

  Gap to close at polyphony 4: 2 704 220 -> 2 031 746 = -672 474 ns (-24.9 %).

  The ladder, costed from the MEASURED stage table (SECTION 1), applied at
  polyphony 4. Every figure marked (proj) is a projection from a standalone
  stage measurement and must be RE-MEASURED before it is believed:

    lever                                    delta ns (N=4) | total     | % of 2 031 746
    ------------------------------------------------------ + --------- + --------------
    (measured, kMaxVoices = 8)                           - | 2 704 220 |   133.1 %
    L-7  kMaxVoices 8 -> 4 (4 spare slots x L)     -50 770 | 2 653 450 |   130.6 %
    L-4  noise 4->2, ecology 6->4, resonance 12->8
         per voice: -68 967 -34 049 -19 040 = -122 056 (proj)
         x 4 voices                                -488 223 | 2 165 227 |   106.6 %
    cheaper material voicing                    unquantified - no measurement exists
    L-3  one body instead of two (body B 34 570/voice)
         x 4 voices                                -138 280 | 2 026 947 |    99.8 %

  So: L-7 + L-4 + L-3 together land 0.2 % under the ceiling ON PROJECTIONS OF
  PROJECTIONS, with no margin whatsoever, and L-3 deletes roadmap line 122's
  multi-body-blend deliverable. L-7 + L-4 alone is 6.6 % short. L-7 alone is
  30.6 % short. There is no lever set short of L-3 that reaches clause (ii) at
  polyphony 4 on these numbers.

  Reducing polyphony below 4 is L-5, whose floor is 4 (spec.md FR-081, L-5) -
  roadmap line 460 says "4-8 voices", so polyphony 2 is OUTSIDE THE ROADMAP and
  needs an explicit recorded amendment, not a quiet reduction inside the build.

================================================================================
SECTION 4 - Q-A, the decision only the user can take (FR-081 L-6 / FR-083)
================================================================================

  Q-A has two halves. NOTHING has been applied and NO baseline has been checked
  in: vorago_engine.h still carries kMaxVoices = 8 (vorago_engine.h:168), the
  VoragoEngine_CpuBudget case does not exist, and spec.md has no SC-001b.

  Q-A.1 - kMaxVoices. Recommendation: lower it to 6, on grounds of honesty
  rather than CPU - it narrows roadmap line 460's "4-8 voices" to "4-6" and is
  therefore a roadmap-touching choice, which is why it is the user's. Measured
  value of the lever: 0.79 % of kReferenceNs at polyphony 4. It changes no
  verdict anywhere in SECTION 2. Keeping 8 costs 50 770 ns/block at polyphony 4
  plus the prepared-but-silent state of four extra voice slots.

  Q-A.2 - shipped polyphony and the lever set. The four honest options:

    (A) Polyphony 4, kMaxVoices 6, NO voicing levers.
        Meets roadmap line 470 (84.5 % of the 30 % ceiling; 25.4 % of a core).
        Does NOT meet SC-001b clause (ii) - baseline 2 839 431 vs 2 133 333.
        Requires the user to rule clause (ii) itself: either SC-001b's baseline
        clause is taken against kReferenceNs, or SC-001b is written as clause
        (i) only. EITHER IS A RELAXATION OF THE REPO CONVENTION and the build
        may not take it - only the user may, recorded in spec.md as the
        amendment.
    (B) Polyphony 4, kMaxVoices 4, L-4 + L-3 applied, then RE-MEASURE.
        Projected 2 026 947 (99.8 % of the clause-(ii) ceiling) - no margin, and
        it costs roadmap line 122's two-body blend plus half the shipped
        source/loop/peak counts, i.e. a sound-design change, not a tuning.
    (C) Polyphony 2, no levers. Passes both clauses with 25 % headroom
        (baseline 1 597 145 = 74.9 % of kMaxAdmissibleNs). Amends roadmap
        line 460's floor - explicitly outside what this spec may choose.
    (D) Polyphony 4, kMaxVoices 6, L-4 only, then RE-MEASURE, and accept
        whatever clause-(ii) residual remains (projected 106.6 %) - i.e. (A)'s
        ruling with a cheaper voice.

  RECOMMENDATION: (A) with Q-A.1 = 6 - ship polyphony 4 at kMaxVoices 6, write
  SC-001b's gate at kReferenceNs, and record explicitly in the amendment that
  the x1.5 regression margin is NOT met at polyphony 4 and why (the alternative
  costs a roadmap deliverable for 0.2 % of projected margin). The measurement
  does not support pretending otherwise, and FR-081 L-6 is exactly this: stop
  and surface.

  WHAT HAPPENS AFTER THE RULING (T031 step 4, currently BLOCKED):
    1. write the ruling into spec.md as SC-001b (polyphony, lever set, and the
       ceiling the gate is taken against);
    2. apply the ruled levers, incl. kMaxVoices in vorago_engine.h:168;
    3. RE-MEASURE - any lever invalidates the table above;
    4. add TEST_CASE("VoragoEngine_CpuBudget", "[systems][vorago][.perf]") to
       vorago_perf_test.cpp with baseline = ceil(re-measured x 1.05) and the
       paired static_assert against the ceiling the ruling names.

